1
00:00:00,636 --> 00:00:06,647
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,663 --> 00:00:09,663
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,663 --> 00:00:10,663
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,663 --> 00:00:11,663
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:07,127
[Episode 5]

6
00:01:11,755 --> 00:01:14,315
Honey, what are you doing?

7
00:01:14,315 --> 00:01:16,231
Oh? You're already up?

8
00:01:16,231 --> 00:01:17,896
Why don't you sleep a little longer?

9
00:01:17,896 --> 00:01:20,547
What is it? Are you making breakfast?

10
00:01:20,547 --> 00:01:22,363
No, sit down first.

11
00:01:22,363 --> 00:01:23,587
Huh?

12
00:01:23,587 --> 00:01:27,127
I woke up early for once,
so I thought I'd show off my skills.

13
00:01:27,127 --> 00:01:29,096
Wow, really?

14
00:01:32,103 --> 00:01:37,730
This boiled egg is just like you,
honest, plain, and exactly as it is.

15
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:41,879
This good-looking fried egg
is just like me, rich and savory,

16
00:01:41,879 --> 00:01:43,796
with a drizzle of sesame oil.

17
00:01:46,319 --> 00:01:48,467
These scrambled eggs are tiny and cute,

18
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:51,695
loaded with butter and milk,
just like our Yul.

19
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:54,383
It's all eggs, isn't it?

20
00:01:54,383 --> 00:01:56,130
No, it's not.

21
00:01:57,839 --> 00:01:58,851
Ta-da!

22
00:01:58,851 --> 00:02:01,179
This colorful salad and sandwich,

23
00:02:01,179 --> 00:02:04,443
with all three of our
unique personalities together.

24
00:02:04,443 --> 00:02:07,131
Wow, my husband is the best, huh?

25
00:02:07,131 --> 00:02:09,359
When did you make all this by yourself?

26
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:11,811
Your mom would faint if she found out.

27
00:02:11,811 --> 00:02:14,659
Gosh, she can never find out.

28
00:02:14,659 --> 00:02:18,830
How am I supposed to
weather the storm if she does?

29
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,930
You seem to be in a really
good mood today, honey.

30
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:23,930
Of course, I am.

31
00:02:23,930 --> 00:02:28,879
I have the two most precious treasures
in the world right here beside me.

32
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:30,839
And speaking of that...

33
00:02:30,839 --> 00:02:32,367
Mommy!

34
00:02:32,367 --> 00:02:33,583
Yul, are you up?

35
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:35,031
Is my baby girl awake?

36
00:02:35,031 --> 00:02:36,963
Did you sleep well?

37
00:02:38,007 --> 00:02:40,691
Daddy made all this breakfast
for you and Mommy. See?

38
00:02:40,691 --> 00:02:43,963
- Let's eat quickly.
- Yay! I'll dig in with Kkongsoon.

39
00:02:43,963 --> 00:02:45,663
Okay.

40
00:02:49,687 --> 00:02:51,496
Kkongsoon?

41
00:02:53,099 --> 00:02:56,830
When did we get a new member
of the family without me knowing?

42
00:02:59,419 --> 00:03:01,359
Yul! Look at this!

43
00:03:01,359 --> 00:03:04,121
Your mommy's friend
sent you a doll as a gift.

44
00:03:04,121 --> 00:03:05,363
Mommy, give it to me.

45
00:03:05,363 --> 00:03:07,096
Here.

46
00:03:08,591 --> 00:03:10,147
Oh, I'm jealous.

47
00:03:10,147 --> 00:03:13,230
You have a friend who even
sends you gifts from overseas.

48
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:15,363
Indeed, having good friends is nice.

49
00:03:15,363 --> 00:03:18,007
Oh, that Russian friend you're close to?

50
00:03:18,007 --> 00:03:19,930
Is the name Seul Gi?

51
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:21,199
Yeah, that's right, Seul Gi.

52
00:03:21,199 --> 00:03:22,979
Come to think of it,
I've never even seen this friend's face.

53
00:03:22,979 --> 00:03:25,496
Seul Gi couldn't come to
our wedding either, right?

54
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:28,223
I'll introduce you
when Seul Gi comes to Korea.

55
00:03:28,223 --> 00:03:30,623
Anyway, I'm grateful to that friend.

56
00:03:30,623 --> 00:03:32,933
Please send Seul Gi my thanks, double for me.

57
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:34,996
I already did right after I got it.

58
00:03:40,107 --> 00:03:42,263
How's the weather over there these days?

59
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,907
Does it rain on and off?

60
00:03:44,907 --> 00:03:46,287
How are you holding up?

61
00:03:46,287 --> 00:03:49,431
You've always hated rain
ever since you were little.

62
00:03:49,431 --> 00:03:52,063
You used to be scared
of thunder and lightning.

63
00:04:01,887 --> 00:04:07,830
If you do this one more time,
I'll deep-fry you with a lightning bolt.

64
00:04:14,531 --> 00:04:16,596
Yul, you shouldn't do that.

65
00:04:16,596 --> 00:04:17,763
Yul, you need to eat this.

66
00:04:17,763 --> 00:04:18,930
No, you can't.

67
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:22,379
Yul, you have to eat!

68
00:04:22,379 --> 00:04:23,903
You need to eat your food.

69
00:04:23,903 --> 00:04:26,296
I'm going to catch you, Yul!

70
00:04:30,382 --> 00:04:32,209
[Not Today]

71
00:04:45,559 --> 00:04:46,830
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

72
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:47,891
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]

73
00:04:55,155 --> 00:04:58,215
<i>Given that Pyo Kyu Cheol
was also killed by a sniper,</i>

74
00:04:58,215 --> 00:05:00,096
<i>should we conclude that the previous
Jeonjak-dong Hotel incident</i>

75
00:05:00,096 --> 00:05:03,143
- <i>was also the work of Kingfisher?</i>
- Oh, my, I knew it was too quiet.

76
00:05:03,143 --> 00:05:05,196
[Can Kingfisher's Return Be Confirmed?]
<i>Of course. Otherwise, how could</i>

77
00:05:05,196 --> 00:05:07,655
- <i>a string of gun murders happen</i>
- You're here?

78
00:05:07,655 --> 00:05:09,630
- <i>in South Korea?</i>
- It was quiet for a few days.

79
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:12,559
- <i>So, the return of Kingfisher is confirmed.</i>
- And now it's dominating the headlines.

80
00:05:12,559 --> 00:05:16,630
At times like this,
whatever article I write gets buried.

81
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:19,251
Whatever I say gets drowned out.

82
00:05:19,251 --> 00:05:23,503
He doesn't even listen to me.
Whatever I say gets buried.

83
00:05:23,503 --> 00:05:25,079
Hey, wait up!

84
00:05:25,079 --> 00:05:29,667
Hey, I heard someone fell
to their death at a construction site.

85
00:05:29,667 --> 00:05:32,196
Oh, my. How did that happen?

86
00:05:32,196 --> 00:05:35,579
The chief wants me to
look into what happened.

87
00:05:35,579 --> 00:05:37,063
Apparently, someone sent in a tip.

88
00:05:37,063 --> 00:05:40,607
"It was an unjust death, reveal the truth,"
and all that nonsense.

89
00:05:40,607 --> 00:05:42,596
Really?

90
00:05:43,735 --> 00:05:48,031
Then dig deep. Fighting.

91
00:05:48,031 --> 00:05:49,563
Here's what I think.

92
00:05:49,563 --> 00:05:50,863
I'd bet this was 100%

93
00:05:50,863 --> 00:05:53,515
an unfortunate accident
caused by safety violations.

94
00:05:53,515 --> 00:05:56,239
If the media starts stirring things up
and digging around,

95
00:05:56,239 --> 00:05:59,311
we could end up bringing down
a perfectly good company

96
00:05:59,311 --> 00:06:01,503
and even causing unexpected ripple effects
on our economy, don't you think?

97
00:06:01,503 --> 00:06:04,127
I wish my colleague Go Ji Soon
would stop talking nonsense

98
00:06:04,127 --> 00:06:08,096
and be faithful to a reporter's
sense of mission and the press's duty.

99
00:06:08,096 --> 00:06:09,763
Well, I have another thought.

100
00:06:09,763 --> 00:06:11,985
If my colleague, Mr. Kwon,

101
00:06:11,985 --> 00:06:15,135
who is always devoted to
his mission and duty as a reporter,

102
00:06:15,135 --> 00:06:18,111
were to investigate this case in my place,

103
00:06:18,111 --> 00:06:22,630
maybe he could "dig into it
much more thoroughly," right?

104
00:06:24,463 --> 00:06:26,463
That's a good idea, huh?

105
00:06:27,896 --> 00:06:29,303
Good idea...

106
00:06:29,303 --> 00:06:31,003
Hey, seriously?

107
00:06:32,467 --> 00:06:35,763
[Seoul Nambu Police Station]
What? A joint investigation?

108
00:06:38,403 --> 00:06:40,471
Whose bright idea was this?

109
00:06:40,471 --> 00:06:43,023
We've reached a preliminary agreement
with the station handling the case.

110
00:06:43,023 --> 00:06:45,430
If you just approve it, Chief...

111
00:06:46,567 --> 00:06:48,335
I told you not to stir things up.

112
00:06:48,335 --> 00:06:52,499
The Pyo Kyu Cheol case is different
from Kingfisher's usual methods.

113
00:06:52,499 --> 00:06:54,463
If we cooperate,
we might be able to find a lead...

114
00:06:54,463 --> 00:06:58,663
I don't see why you need to do this.

115
00:06:58,663 --> 00:07:03,279
That punk's case is finally off my hands.
My 10-year ulcer is healing.

116
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:06,159
Everyone else is desperate
to get that burden off their hands.

117
00:07:06,159 --> 00:07:08,996
What makes you so special?

118
00:07:09,935 --> 00:07:16,539
Are you aiming for a few ranks'
worth of promotions or something?

119
00:07:16,539 --> 00:07:17,907
That's not it.

120
00:07:17,907 --> 00:07:19,727
Then back off.

121
00:07:19,727 --> 00:07:22,527
You know our precinct's performance
is at the bottom this quarter, right?

122
00:07:22,527 --> 00:07:25,523
Instead of worrying about
another precinct's case,

123
00:07:25,523 --> 00:07:28,311
you should nab a few more
petty crooks in our own precinct...

124
00:07:28,311 --> 00:07:30,175
Even one...

125
00:07:30,175 --> 00:07:31,183
Huh?

126
00:07:31,183 --> 00:07:32,883
Wait...

127
00:07:33,691 --> 00:07:36,303
That punk's ignoring me while I'm talking.

128
00:07:36,303 --> 00:07:38,367
I told you to back off, okay?

129
00:07:38,367 --> 00:07:40,427
Beom!

130
00:07:40,427 --> 00:07:45,395
He could say, "Hey, you're that fired up?
Want to suffer a bit more?"

131
00:07:45,395 --> 00:07:47,795
He knows I'll just suffer with no results.

132
00:07:47,795 --> 00:07:50,323
We're not even asking for more personnel.

133
00:07:50,323 --> 00:07:53,163
The Chief is just doing his job.

134
00:07:56,987 --> 00:07:59,731
Why didn't you mention the accidental deaths
of those child sex offenders?

135
00:07:59,731 --> 00:08:02,059
There's no solid evidence.
It's all speculation.

136
00:08:02,059 --> 00:08:06,231
You said you weren't sure if we'd been
barking up the wrong tree or not.

137
00:08:06,231 --> 00:08:10,243
If we're wrong, the eight prior
accidental deaths were all coincidences.

138
00:08:10,243 --> 00:08:13,459
I still can't make sense of it,
even after thinking it over all night.

139
00:08:13,459 --> 00:08:14,696
But if we were right?

140
00:08:14,696 --> 00:08:17,675
Then all the prior deaths were accidents,
and this one was a shooting.

141
00:08:17,675 --> 00:08:18,895
Why on earth?

142
00:08:18,895 --> 00:08:20,475
Why only this time?

143
00:08:20,475 --> 00:08:22,831
Maybe they planned for it to look like
an accident, but something went wrong,

144
00:08:22,831 --> 00:08:25,335
and they had to finish the job with a sniper.

145
00:08:25,335 --> 00:08:28,863
Wow, if that's the case...

146
00:08:28,863 --> 00:08:34,330
Sniping isn't the only method
Kingfisher uses.

147
00:08:34,330 --> 00:08:37,430
Wow, this is getting big.

148
00:08:38,096 --> 00:08:39,330
What are you going to do now?

149
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:41,930
The chief is making a huge fuss
about telling us to back off, isn't he?

150
00:08:48,847 --> 00:08:51,103
You're here?

151
00:08:51,103 --> 00:08:53,663
That guy sent a gift from Russia.

152
00:08:58,379 --> 00:09:00,519
That guy's sticky fingers are still the same.

153
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:02,630
Russian-made stuff is pretty useful.

154
00:09:05,351 --> 00:09:07,383
Let's see if there's
anything worth salvaging.

155
00:09:07,383 --> 00:09:09,193
Looks like that guy's gotten restless again.

156
00:09:09,193 --> 00:09:11,463
I heard that the guy
will be coming to Korea soon.

157
00:09:11,463 --> 00:09:14,415
Gosh, I hate seeing that face.

158
00:09:14,415 --> 00:09:18,931
Yeah? Then I'll have to make sure you don't.

159
00:09:18,931 --> 00:09:22,647
Wow, this thing is still alive? Huh?

160
00:09:22,647 --> 00:09:26,079
I thought it'd suffocate
and die within a few days.

161
00:09:26,079 --> 00:09:28,791
Did you give it some water?

162
00:09:28,791 --> 00:09:31,730
It couldn't have been you taking care of it.

163
00:09:32,391 --> 00:09:34,463
Whoever it was, I'm grateful.

164
00:09:37,107 --> 00:09:40,659
I guess you're alive thanks to this guy, huh?

165
00:09:40,659 --> 00:09:43,091
You've worked hard for three years,
air-purifying plant.

166
00:09:43,091 --> 00:09:44,430
It's Tae Soon.

167
00:09:44,430 --> 00:09:46,896
It's even fresh and lively.

168
00:09:48,843 --> 00:09:52,903
You really have no concept of time,
now or then...

169
00:09:52,903 --> 00:09:56,230
It's April, you know. April.

170
00:09:57,675 --> 00:10:01,319
Being trapped in here like this,
I guess even I would lose track of time...

171
00:10:01,319 --> 00:10:03,196
April...

172
00:10:04,991 --> 00:10:06,859
April...

173
00:10:06,883 --> 00:10:08,139
[Client Meeting Pre-Briefing]

174
00:10:08,139 --> 00:10:10,159
His name is Tak Jong Gu.

175
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:14,159
His dad is a five-term congressman,
and his mom is a chaebol heiress.

176
00:10:14,159 --> 00:10:17,030
He's the notorious youngest son
of the so-called Royal Family.

177
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:18,189
[Client Information: Personal Details]

178
00:10:18,539 --> 00:10:19,683
Let's have something good to drink.

179
00:10:19,683 --> 00:10:21,383
Something fun.

180
00:10:22,283 --> 00:10:25,823
<i>He drugged women, sexually assaulted them,</i>

181
00:10:25,823 --> 00:10:28,575
<i>and even filmed and distributed the footage.</i>

182
00:10:28,575 --> 00:10:32,127
<i>Dozens of videos were found on his computer,</i>

183
00:10:32,127 --> 00:10:35,930
<i>yet he got off with
just a two-year suspended sentence.</i>

184
00:10:36,711 --> 00:10:38,163
A suspended sentence?

185
00:10:38,163 --> 00:10:42,863
He had lawyers from a major law firm
settle with the victims one by one.

186
00:10:42,863 --> 00:10:46,291
Settlement is one way to put it.
It was probably money and threats.

187
00:10:46,291 --> 00:10:48,103
Right now, he's holed up
at the Hongseon casino,

188
00:10:48,103 --> 00:10:50,783
gambling away merrily.

189
00:10:50,783 --> 00:10:53,279
So the Gold class is the type with
a lot of money and connections, huh?

190
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:55,011
The kind who can wriggle out of anything
despite their crimes.

191
00:10:55,011 --> 00:10:57,330
They're the biggest headache.

192
00:10:57,983 --> 00:11:00,696
They're usually heavily guarded,
so getting close to them isn't easy.

193
00:11:00,696 --> 00:11:02,555
And it doesn't come cheap, either.

194
00:11:02,555 --> 00:11:04,799
Especially when we're barely
keeping our operating expenses afloat.

195
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:06,539
- A casino?
- Yeah.

196
00:11:06,539 --> 00:11:11,299
His dad is aiming to become
National Assembly Speaker in a month.

197
00:11:11,299 --> 00:11:13,715
So he was given strict orders to lie low

198
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:16,951
somewhere out of the public eye until then.

199
00:11:16,951 --> 00:11:19,715
Tak Jong Gu is easily excitable
and has weak self-control.

200
00:11:19,715 --> 00:11:23,035
So he's susceptible to gambling addiction.

201
00:11:23,035 --> 00:11:25,047
[Client Information: Criminal History]
He has no sense of guilt, either.

202
00:11:25,047 --> 00:11:27,191
<i>Five years ago, a woman in her twenties</i>

203
00:11:27,191 --> 00:11:29,730
<i>fell to her death from a high-rise apartment.</i>

204
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,763
<i>Tak Jong Gu was there too.</i>

205
00:11:33,375 --> 00:11:34,915
Darn it.

206
00:11:34,915 --> 00:11:36,663
Why were you acting up?

207
00:11:36,663 --> 00:11:39,030
How did he get away with it back then?

208
00:11:40,951 --> 00:11:45,535
He claimed they had a fight and that
she impulsively jumped to her death.

209
00:11:45,535 --> 00:11:50,330
The court acquitted him
due to insufficient evidence.

210
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:54,851
This one's quite an upgrade, huh?

211
00:11:54,851 --> 00:11:56,396
Seems like the world's
getting easier to push around.

212
00:11:56,396 --> 00:11:58,087
[Tak Jong Gu's social media post:
The world is on my side again]

213
00:11:58,111 --> 00:11:58,954
[Law can go to the dogs]

214
00:12:00,683 --> 00:12:03,903
Alright, he's holed up in the provinces.

215
00:12:03,903 --> 00:12:06,475
We'll have to go on a business trip.

216
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:09,530
These days, faking an accidental death

217
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:12,311
with some half-baked scenario
just won't cut it.

218
00:12:12,311 --> 00:12:15,679
We're living in the age of
cutting-edge forensics.

219
00:12:15,679 --> 00:12:20,231
Oh, coming up with a scenario
for every meeting is the hardest part.

220
00:12:20,231 --> 00:12:25,463
Figuring out how to kill someone is
harder than figuring out how to save them.

221
00:12:27,923 --> 00:12:29,863
I'll handle this one.

222
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:32,491
You will, Director Yoo?

223
00:12:33,763 --> 00:12:38,071
But considering the unexpected
Pyo Kyu Cheol incident

224
00:12:38,071 --> 00:12:40,735
stirred up the media and police,

225
00:12:40,735 --> 00:12:44,496
wouldn't it be risky to do
another one right away?

226
00:12:47,715 --> 00:12:51,451
If we're doing it, I hope we hit the jackpot
on the meeting day.

227
00:12:51,451 --> 00:12:56,296
Make the day of greatest joy
become his ancestral rite day, right?

228
00:13:01,323 --> 00:13:03,023
Ancestral rite...

229
00:13:05,607 --> 00:13:07,330
What day is it today?

230
00:13:09,498 --> 00:13:11,891
[Mother]

231
00:13:16,507 --> 00:13:19,063
Hello, Mother.

232
00:13:20,839 --> 00:13:23,599
Of course, I know.

233
00:13:23,599 --> 00:13:25,299
Yeah.

234
00:13:32,547 --> 00:13:34,067
Assistant Manager Yang,
I still have my half-day off, right?

235
00:13:34,067 --> 00:13:37,696
Please. We'll continue
the meeting tomorrow. Sorry.

236
00:13:43,183 --> 00:13:46,207
Director Yoo must attend
the ancestral rite at her in-laws' house.

237
00:13:46,207 --> 00:13:47,563
Of course, she does.
She's the daughter-in-law.

238
00:13:47,563 --> 00:13:49,995
So Kingfisher has become
a daughter-in-law now too.

239
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,755
On a day like this, isn't she less
a daughter-in-law and more a servant?

240
00:13:51,755 --> 00:13:53,930
I should probably come with her...

241
00:14:12,939 --> 00:14:14,403
I think this is the place.

242
00:14:14,427 --> 00:14:19,161
[My Safety, My Coworkers' Safety]

243
00:14:24,551 --> 00:14:26,597
<i>Two weeks ago, a worker fell to his death</i>

244
00:14:26,597 --> 00:14:28,771
<i>while organizing materials
on the sixth floor.</i>

245
00:14:28,771 --> 00:14:30,779
<i>The investigation concluded
that it was an accident</i>

246
00:14:30,779 --> 00:14:34,104
<i>caused by his own negligence, correct?</i>

247
00:14:34,104 --> 00:14:36,463
That's what's been made public.

248
00:14:36,463 --> 00:14:37,659
Now we need to find out for ourselves.

249
00:14:37,659 --> 00:14:43,196
Whether it was just an accident
or an unjust death disguised as one.

250
00:14:43,196 --> 00:14:45,619
While everyone's
focused on the Kingfisher case,

251
00:14:45,619 --> 00:14:47,047
we'll investigate the unjust death of

252
00:14:47,047 --> 00:14:50,896
the socially vulnerable
left in the blind spot?

253
00:14:52,296 --> 00:14:54,215
I really like this kind of stuff.

254
00:14:54,215 --> 00:14:57,063
This is what being a reporter is all about.

255
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,796
Let's go, Mr. Kwon.

256
00:15:05,807 --> 00:15:08,295
I mean, the police already came and went.

257
00:15:08,295 --> 00:15:11,935
The Ministry of Employment and Labor
and the Ministry of Land investigated too.

258
00:15:11,935 --> 00:15:15,683
It was all determined
to be personal negligence.

259
00:15:15,683 --> 00:15:20,299
Really? Then what were the names
of the officials who came out that day?

260
00:15:20,299 --> 00:15:22,730
Well, still, our chairman said

261
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:26,027
the company had a moral obligation,
so we covered workers' compensation,

262
00:15:26,027 --> 00:15:30,596
the death benefit, and even added
a hefty condolence payment.

263
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:36,395
There's no one as generous as our chairman.

264
00:15:36,395 --> 00:15:37,803
I see.

265
00:15:37,803 --> 00:15:41,996
I'll ask the chairman about that myself.
Where can I meet him?

266
00:15:42,647 --> 00:15:47,207
Well, it's rather difficult
to meet the chairman in person.

267
00:15:47,207 --> 00:15:51,539
Then what about the coworkers who worked
with the deceased, Kang Yeong Ho?

268
00:15:51,539 --> 00:15:53,659
Oh, that's possible.

269
00:15:53,659 --> 00:15:55,099
Oh, there's one right over there.

270
00:15:55,099 --> 00:15:57,730
- Mr. Park Chun Bok!
- Yes.

271
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:01,263
Go talk to him.

272
00:16:06,047 --> 00:16:09,715
That fellow Kang Yeong Ho,
he reeked of alcohol that day.

273
00:16:09,715 --> 00:16:14,359
I don't know if he'd been drinking
all morning or was still hungover.

274
00:16:14,359 --> 00:16:16,618
It had happened a few times before too.

275
00:16:16,618 --> 00:16:20,330
That day too, he didn't wear his hard hat,
so I warned him several times.

276
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:22,171
Yeah.

277
00:16:22,171 --> 00:16:23,495
I see.

278
00:16:23,495 --> 00:16:27,390
Did you report that to the company as well?

279
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:31,930
Do you think I feel good talking about
a former colleague like that?

280
00:16:31,930 --> 00:16:33,915
Besides, he's dead.

281
00:16:33,915 --> 00:16:37,111
Still, I thought I should be honest
about what happened.

282
00:16:37,111 --> 00:16:40,151
- Yeah.
- Of course, you should have.

283
00:16:40,151 --> 00:16:44,247
Even after all that, the chairman
was incredibly generous, wasn't he?

284
00:16:44,247 --> 00:16:45,553
Yeah.

285
00:16:45,553 --> 00:16:48,563
So everyone seems pretty grateful
to the chairman.

286
00:16:48,563 --> 00:16:51,007
We were at a loss
because the construction was delayed too.

287
00:16:51,007 --> 00:16:55,396
The chairman even made sure
we got our wages in advance.

288
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:04,551
I mean, the company
processed the industrial accident,

289
00:17:04,551 --> 00:17:07,275
paid the compensation,
and even gave a condolence payment.

290
00:17:07,275 --> 00:17:10,203
Didn't they do everything
they were supposed to?

291
00:17:10,203 --> 00:17:13,451
That's not something companies usually do.

292
00:17:13,451 --> 00:17:15,265
You know it well.

293
00:17:15,265 --> 00:17:16,363
Pardon?

294
00:17:16,363 --> 00:17:20,451
He smelled of alcohol
and wasn't wearing a hard hat.

295
00:17:20,451 --> 00:17:21,691
In such cases, companies usually

296
00:17:21,691 --> 00:17:24,163
highlight personal negligence
and cut ties without mercy.

297
00:17:24,163 --> 00:17:26,196
That's how companies operate.

298
00:17:26,855 --> 00:17:31,363
But the chairman stepped in
and went all out with compensation?

299
00:17:31,363 --> 00:17:36,339
And this so-called witness
just happens to show up

300
00:17:36,339 --> 00:17:39,007
and start talking about
the victim's negligence.

301
00:17:39,007 --> 00:17:41,523
Oh, you're right.

302
00:17:41,523 --> 00:17:43,131
So what do we do now?

303
00:17:43,131 --> 00:17:45,071
We don't even know
who the informant is, do we?

304
00:17:45,071 --> 00:17:46,771
Well, that's...

305
00:17:48,754 --> 00:17:50,505
[Receive Gaecheon Construction
Meal Tickets Here]

306
00:17:50,779 --> 00:17:53,663
Let's grab some food first
and look into it afterward.

307
00:17:53,663 --> 00:17:56,796
We're eating again?
We just ate before we came.

308
00:18:00,655 --> 00:18:03,071
- Take a look before you go.
- I'll be right back.

309
00:18:03,071 --> 00:18:05,747
- Yeah.
- It's been a while.

310
00:18:05,747 --> 00:18:07,451
You know we're not serving
steamed rice cake, right?

311
00:18:07,451 --> 00:18:10,153
- You're here?
- Oh, really? Hello.

312
00:18:10,153 --> 00:18:12,015
Hey, I'm here.

313
00:18:12,015 --> 00:18:13,763
Oh, Tae Seong's family is here.

314
00:18:13,763 --> 00:18:14,896
The baby's mom came too?

315
00:18:14,896 --> 00:18:16,311
Yeah, have you been well?

316
00:18:16,311 --> 00:18:17,415
Welcome.

317
00:18:17,415 --> 00:18:22,063
Seeing you bring your daughter-in-law,
it must be an ancestral rite day.

318
00:18:22,063 --> 00:18:25,435
Don't make that delicate daughter-in-law
do all the work every time.

319
00:18:25,435 --> 00:18:27,099
Bring that precious son of yours too.

320
00:18:27,099 --> 00:18:29,721
Oh, please. Why would my son come here?

321
00:18:29,721 --> 00:18:31,938
He's busy working at the company.

322
00:18:31,938 --> 00:18:35,419
Anyway, you're always going on
about your son, all year round.

323
00:18:35,419 --> 00:18:38,507
So, what kind of fish are you making?

324
00:18:38,507 --> 00:18:42,487
- Hey, you pick one out.
- What?

325
00:18:42,487 --> 00:18:45,996
Pick out what you think we should buy.

326
00:18:47,303 --> 00:18:49,996
Oh, okay.

327
00:18:54,891 --> 00:18:55,903
How about this, Mother?

328
00:18:55,903 --> 00:18:57,127
Oh, my.

329
00:18:57,127 --> 00:18:59,137
- Oh, what am I going to do?
- It's so shiny.

330
00:18:59,137 --> 00:19:01,095
Oh, jeez.

331
00:19:01,095 --> 00:19:04,930
Hey, I told you clearly that fish
whose names end in "chi" are low-grade

332
00:19:04,930 --> 00:19:08,732
and shouldn't go on
the memorial table, didn't I?

333
00:19:08,732 --> 00:19:11,817
How can you keep doing this
when I've told you so many times?

334
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,255
Oh, jeez.

335
00:19:14,255 --> 00:19:16,696
She never told me that.

336
00:19:18,935 --> 00:19:22,730
I'm sorry, Mother. I'll make sure
to remember from now on.

337
00:19:22,730 --> 00:19:27,830
Then, among the ones
that don't end in "chi"...

338
00:19:28,829 --> 00:19:30,123
This is a croaker, right?

339
00:19:30,123 --> 00:19:32,147
Yeah, croaker!

340
00:19:32,147 --> 00:19:34,530
This one's saury?

341
00:19:35,491 --> 00:19:37,179
And that one is mackerel?

342
00:19:37,179 --> 00:19:38,611
And this one's pomfret!

343
00:19:38,611 --> 00:19:40,163
Am I right, Mother?

344
00:19:40,163 --> 00:19:44,030
Oh, my, now you know it perfectly
without even being told?

345
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:47,267
So, we can't have saury and mackerel,
which end in "chi,"

346
00:19:47,267 --> 00:19:50,863
so please give me pomfret and croaker,
which don't end in "chi."

347
00:19:50,863 --> 00:19:51,967
Oh, okay.

348
00:19:51,967 --> 00:19:54,230
- And some abalone too.
- Okay.

349
00:20:02,163 --> 00:20:05,131
Kang Yeong Ho? He was drinking?

350
00:20:05,131 --> 00:20:07,883
Oh, my, where did you hear such nonsense?

351
00:20:07,883 --> 00:20:11,618
Right? See? I told you it wasn't true.

352
00:20:11,618 --> 00:20:14,467
- Pardon?
- I mean, she kept insisting that

353
00:20:14,467 --> 00:20:16,167
everyone at the construction site drinks,

354
00:20:16,167 --> 00:20:20,563
and that Kang Yeong Ho caused the accident
because he was still drunk that day.

355
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:24,630
Oh, that's right. I remember now.

356
00:20:24,630 --> 00:20:27,879
I had a bit of a preconceived notion.

357
00:20:27,879 --> 00:20:30,863
You shouldn't make someone
so wrongfully accused like that.

358
00:20:30,863 --> 00:20:33,596
That man never even touched alcohol.

359
00:20:33,596 --> 00:20:39,067
Even when he had something really upsetting
going on, I never saw him drink.

360
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:40,331
Something upsetting?

361
00:20:40,331 --> 00:20:45,119
Yeah, I heard something happened to his wife.

362
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:49,471
That guy absolutely adored his wife.

363
00:20:49,471 --> 00:20:52,555
As they say these days,
he was a total wife guy.

364
00:20:52,555 --> 00:20:56,663
Oh, sounds just like me.

365
00:20:59,047 --> 00:21:04,727
Wait, now that I think about it, his wife
used to work at the chairman's house.

366
00:21:04,727 --> 00:21:07,530
That's enough, right? Enjoy your meal.

367
00:21:10,343 --> 00:21:12,263
The chairman's house?

368
00:21:22,627 --> 00:21:24,479
- Oh, my.
- They're here.

369
00:21:24,479 --> 00:21:26,507
Mommy!

370
00:21:26,507 --> 00:21:28,199
Yul, what were you playing?

371
00:21:28,199 --> 00:21:32,687
I was playing with Auntie,
Kkongsoon, and Chiba.

372
00:21:32,687 --> 00:21:36,686
Oh, my sister-in-law had to
play pack mule again.

373
00:21:36,686 --> 00:21:39,054
- Jeez!
- Quit nagging and just take the bags.

374
00:21:39,054 --> 00:21:42,330
I'm doing it. I'm doing it.

375
00:21:56,223 --> 00:21:57,843
[Three Years Ago]
Hey!

376
00:21:57,843 --> 00:22:00,408
Have you never chopped an onion before?

377
00:22:00,408 --> 00:22:02,930
Why are you using the knife like that?

378
00:22:02,930 --> 00:22:04,733
Are you cutting a cake or something?

379
00:22:04,733 --> 00:22:07,963
I'm just not used to using it
for this kind of thing.

380
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:11,807
[Two Years Ago]

381
00:22:13,491 --> 00:22:15,499
Wait, why is this here?

382
00:22:15,499 --> 00:22:18,630
Do we have any Southeast Asian ancestors?

383
00:22:19,259 --> 00:22:21,530
I just bought it for you to try.

384
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:23,727
[One Year Ago]

385
00:22:23,727 --> 00:22:25,080
Hey!

386
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:27,443
Did you mix grains into the rice?

387
00:22:27,443 --> 00:22:30,143
For the rice we're putting
on the memorial table?

388
00:22:30,143 --> 00:22:32,123
They say it's good for your health...

389
00:22:32,123 --> 00:22:36,730
Wow, jeez. You're driving me crazy. Really.

390
00:22:49,987 --> 00:22:52,035
Okay!

391
00:22:52,035 --> 00:22:53,735
Should I give it a try?

392
00:23:08,987 --> 00:23:12,455
Hey, did you put garlic
in the seasoned vegetables?

393
00:23:12,455 --> 00:23:14,863
Yes, Mother, for a deeper flavor...

394
00:23:16,063 --> 00:23:18,696
Wait... All of that too?

395
00:23:20,287 --> 00:23:22,818
Mother, I put it in all of...

396
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:24,323
I'm sorry, Mother. Oh, no.

397
00:23:24,323 --> 00:23:27,518
Oh, I'll go right now and buy them again.

398
00:23:27,518 --> 00:23:28,923
I'm sorry.

399
00:23:28,923 --> 00:23:32,163
What are we going to do with all this?

400
00:23:32,783 --> 00:23:34,155
I'll be back.

401
00:23:34,155 --> 00:23:36,097
- Wow, seriously...
- Jeez.

402
00:23:36,097 --> 00:23:39,068
Putting garlic
in ancestral rite vegetables...

403
00:23:39,068 --> 00:23:41,506
No matter how clueless she is,
that's too much.

404
00:23:41,506 --> 00:23:45,083
- It's too much, too much.
- Come on. She might not know.

405
00:23:45,083 --> 00:23:46,443
It's no big deal.

406
00:23:46,443 --> 00:23:48,895
It's because she's an orphan.

407
00:23:48,895 --> 00:23:51,895
She never had parents
to teach her these things.

408
00:23:51,895 --> 00:23:54,327
I knew that line was coming.

409
00:23:54,327 --> 00:23:56,827
You really found your opening, Mom.

410
00:23:56,827 --> 00:23:58,930
Be quiet, you girl!

411
00:24:01,055 --> 00:24:05,243
[Kang Yeong Ho]

412
00:24:09,443 --> 00:24:10,843
<i>Tae Seong, when are you coming?</i>

413
00:24:10,843 --> 00:24:12,543
Is anyone home?

414
00:24:18,851 --> 00:24:20,730
Hello?

415
00:24:22,619 --> 00:24:24,595
I guess no one's here.

416
00:24:24,595 --> 00:24:28,339
Do you really think
Kang Yeong Ho's wife is the informant?

417
00:24:28,339 --> 00:24:30,163
What's the matter?

418
00:24:30,163 --> 00:24:32,855
They moved out. No one lives there now.

419
00:24:32,855 --> 00:24:34,583
They moved? When?

420
00:24:34,583 --> 00:24:36,796
I think it was the day
of the husband's funeral.

421
00:24:36,796 --> 00:24:39,851
They seemed to be in a hurry
and called a moving truck that night.

422
00:24:39,851 --> 00:24:42,703
Do you happen to have
the wife's contact information?

423
00:24:42,703 --> 00:24:45,275
No, we're not close enough
to have each other's numbers.

424
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:47,687
Is there a real estate office nearby?

425
00:24:47,687 --> 00:24:48,863
A real estate office?

426
00:24:48,863 --> 00:24:50,935
Oh, I guess you're here to look at the house.

427
00:24:50,935 --> 00:24:54,159
Go out of this alley
and turn the corner. It's right there.

428
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:55,996
Okay, thank you.

429
00:24:58,387 --> 00:24:59,743
Why the real estate office?

430
00:24:59,743 --> 00:25:02,163
If she left in such a hurry, she probably
couldn't even get her deposit back.

431
00:25:02,163 --> 00:25:03,530
She'll have to contact them
eventually, right?

432
00:25:03,530 --> 00:25:04,579
What is she talking about?

433
00:25:04,579 --> 00:25:07,479
<i>Bo Na is going through a rough time.
She's become Mom's lackey.</i>

434
00:25:07,479 --> 00:25:10,047
<i>Tae Seong, you didn't forget about
the ancestral rite today, did you?</i>

435
00:25:10,047 --> 00:25:11,171
Oh!

436
00:25:11,171 --> 00:25:12,607
What is it? What's wrong, Mr. Kwon?

437
00:25:12,607 --> 00:25:13,851
What time is it now?

438
00:25:13,851 --> 00:25:15,171
Right now?

439
00:25:15,171 --> 00:25:16,871
Oh!

440
00:25:17,292 --> 00:25:21,755
Oh, my, I can't live
a long life like this. Jeez.

441
00:25:24,539 --> 00:25:25,336
[I'm in Gangwon Province right now,
but I'll get there as soon as I can]

442
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:27,288
Gangwon Province?

443
00:25:27,288 --> 00:25:30,588
Oh, my, if he leaves now,
when is he supposed to get here?

444
00:25:31,452 --> 00:25:34,321
Auntie, what's an ancestral rite?

445
00:25:35,294 --> 00:25:37,870
Yul, do you want to know
what an ancestral rite is?

446
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:40,178
An ancestral rite is...

447
00:25:40,178 --> 00:25:42,086
when people who have gone to heaven

448
00:25:42,086 --> 00:25:46,546
come over to our house to eat,
have fun, and then go back.

449
00:25:46,546 --> 00:25:48,598
What is an orphan?

450
00:25:48,598 --> 00:25:50,298
Huh?

451
00:25:52,530 --> 00:25:56,450
Anyway, Mom said that in front of the child.

452
00:25:56,450 --> 00:25:59,626
That's for parents...

453
00:25:59,626 --> 00:26:05,690
Well, it means Yul's mommy's parents
have passed away.

454
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:08,007
Is Mommy an orphan?

455
00:26:09,750 --> 00:26:13,974
Yes. Her parents went to heaven
a very long time ago.

456
00:26:13,974 --> 00:26:16,541
Then are they coming over for dinner today?

457
00:26:18,054 --> 00:26:23,206
No. The people coming today are someone else.

458
00:26:23,206 --> 00:26:24,206
Why aren't they coming?

459
00:26:24,206 --> 00:26:27,594
Well... Maybe because they weren't invited?

460
00:26:27,594 --> 00:26:28,902
Then when are they coming?

461
00:26:28,902 --> 00:26:31,038
Oh, well...

462
00:26:31,038 --> 00:26:32,738
If you call them?

463
00:26:35,226 --> 00:26:37,854
They'll come if you call them.

464
00:26:37,854 --> 00:26:40,907
Like, "Please come quickly."

465
00:26:46,158 --> 00:26:47,174
Yul's mommy!

466
00:26:47,174 --> 00:26:48,105
[Ok's Flower Shop]

467
00:26:49,042 --> 00:26:52,141
- Oh, my, ma'am!
- What brings you here at this hour?

468
00:26:55,082 --> 00:26:57,470
Do you have a minute right now?

469
00:26:57,470 --> 00:26:59,670
- Me?
- Yeah.

470
00:26:59,670 --> 00:27:00,946
Right now?

471
00:27:00,946 --> 00:27:03,954
Well... I have to go.

472
00:27:03,954 --> 00:27:06,007
What's going on? Why?

473
00:27:13,862 --> 00:27:15,507
- I'm here.
- Daddy!

474
00:27:15,507 --> 00:27:16,966
Yul!

475
00:27:16,966 --> 00:27:19,134
What? You got here sooner than I expected.

476
00:27:19,134 --> 00:27:20,326
Did you speed all the way here?

477
00:27:20,326 --> 00:27:21,974
Where's Bo Na?
She wasn't answering her phone.

478
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:25,338
She's on the veranda. And as you can see,
she couldn't answer the phone.

479
00:27:25,338 --> 00:27:26,482
Since the afternoon, all day...

480
00:27:26,482 --> 00:27:28,450
So why was she here all day? What about work?

481
00:27:28,450 --> 00:27:30,362
She took a half-day off.
I guess Mom called her.

482
00:27:30,362 --> 00:27:31,566
Mom's resting in the master bedroom.

483
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:34,890
- Let's go, Yul! Let's go with Auntie.
- Let's go.

484
00:27:34,890 --> 00:27:37,274
Let's go! Want to draw?

485
00:27:40,798 --> 00:27:43,170
- Honey!
- You're here?

486
00:27:43,170 --> 00:27:46,206
You should have told me.
I almost completely forgot.

487
00:27:46,206 --> 00:27:48,207
Sorry. I forgot too.

488
00:27:49,586 --> 00:27:51,386
Oh, my, really, Mom...

489
00:27:51,386 --> 00:27:53,282
Why did she call someone who works
at a company out in the afternoon?

490
00:27:53,282 --> 00:27:55,806
Come on, it's just one day.
Why are you making a fuss?

491
00:27:55,806 --> 00:27:56,946
There's just a little cleanup left.

492
00:27:56,946 --> 00:27:58,462
It's all done. It's all done.

493
00:27:58,462 --> 00:27:59,506
Rest. I'll do it.

494
00:27:59,506 --> 00:28:01,686
No, don't say things like that.
Just sit over there.

495
00:28:01,686 --> 00:28:04,274
I can finish it quickly before Mom comes out.

496
00:28:07,798 --> 00:28:09,694
- Huh?
- Did you get hurt?

497
00:28:09,694 --> 00:28:14,386
Yeah, I scratched myself while cleaning
the abalone earlier. It was bleeding...

498
00:28:14,386 --> 00:28:15,906
Stay right there.

499
00:28:15,906 --> 00:28:18,574
I put some medicine on it. Honey, it's okay.

500
00:28:21,698 --> 00:28:23,478
I'm okay.

501
00:28:23,478 --> 00:28:25,341
I'm not okay.

502
00:28:28,318 --> 00:28:30,141
It must hurt.

503
00:28:47,242 --> 00:28:49,450
There, done.

504
00:28:49,450 --> 00:28:51,068
It clings just like skin.

505
00:28:51,068 --> 00:28:54,434
You put it on so well
that it's like it's not even there.

506
00:28:54,434 --> 00:28:56,814
And it's easy to move around with.

507
00:28:56,814 --> 00:28:58,162
Thanks.

508
00:28:58,162 --> 00:28:59,214
I should get back to work.

509
00:28:59,214 --> 00:29:00,574
Oh, I told you, it's fine.

510
00:29:00,574 --> 00:29:02,274
Why?

511
00:29:03,190 --> 00:29:04,262
No.

512
00:29:04,262 --> 00:29:05,822
I can just quickly finish
before Mom comes out.

513
00:29:05,822 --> 00:29:08,522
- I'll get in trouble.
- It's okay.

514
00:29:08,522 --> 00:29:11,274
No, she's scary.

515
00:29:18,174 --> 00:29:20,174
Please get some rest.

516
00:29:32,586 --> 00:29:34,286
Mother!

517
00:29:43,326 --> 00:29:44,974
Let's go. Let's go.

518
00:29:44,974 --> 00:29:45,974
It's Yul!

519
00:29:45,974 --> 00:29:48,014
- Yul!
- Auntie!

520
00:29:48,014 --> 00:29:50,062
- When did you get here?
- Have you been well?

521
00:29:50,062 --> 00:29:51,594
How did you two get here together?

522
00:29:51,594 --> 00:29:53,466
Du Ri stopped by the shop and gave me a ride.

523
00:29:53,466 --> 00:29:55,278
What about you? Where are you taking Yul?

524
00:29:55,278 --> 00:29:58,807
Oh, we're going for a walk to the playground.

525
00:29:58,807 --> 00:30:00,141
Really? Oh, my, that sounds nice.

526
00:30:00,141 --> 00:30:01,705
Go on ahead, okay?

527
00:30:01,705 --> 00:30:05,118
- Be careful.
- Careful, careful.

528
00:30:05,118 --> 00:30:06,626
- Evacuate.
- Evacuate?

529
00:30:06,626 --> 00:30:07,742
- Oh, my.
- Why?

530
00:30:07,742 --> 00:30:10,907
It's obvious. Mom's giving
her daughter-in-law a hard time again.

531
00:30:12,566 --> 00:30:15,274
What's it this time?
What's she unhappy about now?

532
00:30:15,274 --> 00:30:18,741
Tae Seong got caught
doing the dishes in the kitchen.

533
00:30:18,741 --> 00:30:19,741
Oh, my.

534
00:30:19,741 --> 00:30:20,814
What?

535
00:30:20,814 --> 00:30:22,874
Take that off. Take it off.

536
00:30:22,874 --> 00:30:24,207
- I said take it off!
- Oh, I'm done.

537
00:30:24,207 --> 00:30:26,370
Take it off, got it?

538
00:30:26,370 --> 00:30:28,770
Did I raise you like that?

539
00:30:28,770 --> 00:30:32,078
I raised you without ever
making you lift a finger.

540
00:30:32,078 --> 00:30:34,141
I'm sorry, Mother.

541
00:30:34,141 --> 00:30:36,086
- I...
- Mom.

542
00:30:36,086 --> 00:30:38,359
She's been working all day.
I just told her to rest a bit.

543
00:30:38,359 --> 00:30:41,278
How much work could she possibly have done?

544
00:30:41,278 --> 00:30:43,906
Hey, come out. You, come here!

545
00:30:43,906 --> 00:30:48,707
Do you usually make
our Tae Seong do housework?

546
00:30:50,654 --> 00:30:55,002
No, what housework? I do housework?

547
00:30:55,002 --> 00:30:57,607
Bossing him around. You made him.

548
00:30:57,607 --> 00:30:59,046
No wonder.

549
00:30:59,046 --> 00:31:02,102
You looked way too practiced
for this to be your first time.

550
00:31:02,102 --> 00:31:05,562
Last time, too, when she was away
using work as an excuse,

551
00:31:05,562 --> 00:31:07,494
you cooked and cleaned up after her.

552
00:31:07,494 --> 00:31:09,807
I didn't say anything then,
but I was furious.

553
00:31:09,807 --> 00:31:11,874
- Mom! That was me...
- Mom, we're here.

554
00:31:11,874 --> 00:31:13,441
We brought kimchi.

555
00:31:13,441 --> 00:31:14,441
- You're here?
- Guys.

556
00:31:14,441 --> 00:31:16,454
You had a hard time, right?

557
00:31:16,454 --> 00:31:19,507
Good grief, Tae Seong is doing the dishes.

558
00:31:19,507 --> 00:31:22,446
He never once set foot in the kitchen.

559
00:31:22,446 --> 00:31:25,202
Imagine how much pressure
she must've put on him.

560
00:31:25,202 --> 00:31:27,598
Goodness, what on earth is going on?

561
00:31:27,598 --> 00:31:29,142
Mom, she hurt her hand.

562
00:31:29,142 --> 00:31:31,814
How did her perfectly fine hand
suddenly get hurt?

563
00:31:31,814 --> 00:31:32,907
She's faking it
because she doesn't want to work.

564
00:31:32,907 --> 00:31:34,614
You're hurt?

565
00:31:34,614 --> 00:31:36,474
- No, I'm fine.
- You should've been more careful.

566
00:31:36,474 --> 00:31:38,598
- Just a little. This tiny bit.
- Oh, dear.

567
00:31:38,598 --> 00:31:40,741
- Are you okay?
- Now that we're all gathered.

568
00:31:42,310 --> 00:31:45,894
Let's settle this once and for all.

569
00:31:45,894 --> 00:31:48,286
- What?
- Here's what I think.

570
00:31:48,286 --> 00:31:50,542
Settle what?
Honey, what are you talking about?

571
00:31:50,542 --> 00:31:52,578
- Don't do this.
- I think that...

572
00:31:52,578 --> 00:31:53,708
it's our family's ancestral rite,

573
00:31:53,708 --> 00:31:55,282
yet you're making
the daughter-in-law do all the work?

574
00:31:55,282 --> 00:31:57,666
I think this is unfair.

575
00:31:57,666 --> 00:32:01,341
Times have changed,
so men should help out too.

576
00:32:01,341 --> 00:32:03,134
And she's going back to work now too.

577
00:32:03,134 --> 00:32:06,706
So, from now on, I'll come early
and help out more. Okay?

578
00:32:06,706 --> 00:32:08,834
- No.
- What a load of nonsense.

579
00:32:08,834 --> 00:32:10,526
Who says anyone's doing anything?

580
00:32:10,526 --> 00:32:11,650
Jeez.

581
00:32:11,650 --> 00:32:16,426
Why are you suddenly acting like this
when you've always listened to Mom?

582
00:32:16,426 --> 00:32:18,143
And from now on,
you should come early and help too.

583
00:32:18,143 --> 00:32:21,018
Don't leave it all to Bo Na.

584
00:32:21,018 --> 00:32:23,341
Kwon Tae Seong, you're being ridiculous.

585
00:32:23,341 --> 00:32:25,770
Sun Il, that's not what he...

586
00:32:25,770 --> 00:32:26,770
Oh, I'm sorry.

587
00:32:26,770 --> 00:32:29,422
It's fine when Mom and your sisters
work themselves to death,

588
00:32:29,422 --> 00:32:32,874
but you can't stand
seeing your wife struggle?

589
00:32:32,874 --> 00:32:35,674
- That's not what I meant...
- Oh, both of you, stop it.

590
00:32:35,674 --> 00:32:37,950
Tae Seong isn't wrong about a single thing.

591
00:32:37,950 --> 00:32:40,841
He finally came to his senses. Good for him.

592
00:32:40,841 --> 00:32:43,498
The timing is just annoying.

593
00:32:43,498 --> 00:32:46,000
He acted like he didn't know all this time,
but why is he doing this now?

594
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:49,774
What do you think?
It's all because his wife put him up to it.

595
00:32:49,774 --> 00:32:52,741
Oh, my poor son.
What am I going to do with my son now?

596
00:32:52,741 --> 00:32:55,034
Oh, Mom, enough with the "my son" routine.

597
00:32:55,034 --> 00:32:59,596
These days, it's not normal for one woman
to shoulder all the housework alone.

598
00:32:59,596 --> 00:33:02,739
While we're at it, let's get rid of
this outdated ancestral rite too, yeah?

599
00:33:02,739 --> 00:33:03,913
Huh?

600
00:33:03,913 --> 00:33:05,297
Shut your mouth, you girl!

601
00:33:05,297 --> 00:33:06,974
Stay out of it.

602
00:33:06,974 --> 00:33:10,367
Hey, if you have a mouth, say something.

603
00:33:10,367 --> 00:33:12,430
Is that how your parents raised you?

604
00:33:12,430 --> 00:33:14,274
- Mom!
- Mom!

605
00:33:25,474 --> 00:33:29,142
Honey, put on your coat. Let's go home.

606
00:33:37,734 --> 00:33:40,322
Yul, be careful not to get hurt.

607
00:33:40,322 --> 00:33:42,022
Okay.

608
00:33:44,050 --> 00:33:47,634
Kwon Se Ah, who never cared
what anyone thought,

609
00:33:47,634 --> 00:33:49,734
is actually worried about what a kid thinks.

610
00:33:49,734 --> 00:33:52,407
Parenting is hard, indeed.

611
00:33:54,448 --> 00:33:56,454
I wonder if she's finally calmed down.

612
00:33:56,454 --> 00:33:58,600
What did you just say?

613
00:33:58,600 --> 00:33:59,707
We're not participating
in the ancestral rites anymore.

614
00:33:59,707 --> 00:34:01,930
What are you doing? I said put on your coat.

615
00:34:01,930 --> 00:34:03,826
What are you saying you won't do?

616
00:34:03,826 --> 00:34:05,441
- Oh, my.
- Mother!

617
00:34:05,441 --> 00:34:07,174
Mom, Mom...

618
00:34:08,590 --> 00:34:11,370
I think I was being short-sighted.

619
00:34:11,370 --> 00:34:14,314
I used to think
going along with everything you said

620
00:34:14,314 --> 00:34:18,282
was the best way to keep the peace,
but not anymore.

621
00:34:18,282 --> 00:34:24,118
Just as I'm your precious son,
she's my precious wife.

622
00:34:24,118 --> 00:34:27,838
Mom, I'm so scared that one day
she might suddenly disappear from my side.

623
00:34:27,838 --> 00:34:31,470
Just imagining it makes me
feel like I can't breathe.

624
00:34:31,470 --> 00:34:33,118
She is my precious family.

625
00:34:33,118 --> 00:34:37,441
So please, don't ever treat my wife
or my family that way again.

626
00:34:39,607 --> 00:34:43,707
- Unbelievable, that... that punk...
- Mom, Mom!

627
00:34:50,230 --> 00:34:51,930
This...

628
00:34:53,786 --> 00:34:55,641
Why am I...

629
00:34:58,330 --> 00:35:00,174
How did I...

630
00:35:01,458 --> 00:35:03,341
Mother, I'm sorry.

631
00:35:03,341 --> 00:35:05,641
I'm sorry. I shouldn't be receiving this...

632
00:35:07,826 --> 00:35:10,698
Wait... Hey, Kwon Tae Seong!

633
00:35:10,698 --> 00:35:12,407
Aren't you coming here?

634
00:35:12,407 --> 00:35:13,841
- Mom.
- Aren't you coming here?

635
00:35:13,841 --> 00:35:15,607
What are you really trying to do?

636
00:35:15,607 --> 00:35:17,441
- Apologize to your mom.
- What's wrong with you?

637
00:35:17,441 --> 00:35:18,541
And why are you acting like this too?

638
00:35:18,541 --> 00:35:19,741
You're just going to leave after this?

639
00:35:19,741 --> 00:35:21,074
Why are you picking up the dried pollock?

640
00:35:21,074 --> 00:35:22,407
You're just going to leave like this?

641
00:35:22,407 --> 00:35:24,838
- Hurry up and say you're sorry.
- You have no manners.

642
00:35:24,838 --> 00:35:26,194
Oh, stop.

643
00:35:26,194 --> 00:35:27,874
- Stop it!
- You dare?

644
00:35:27,874 --> 00:35:29,014
- You little punk!
- Mom?

645
00:35:29,014 --> 00:35:30,798
- Mom!
- Oh, my!

646
00:35:30,798 --> 00:35:31,807
Are you okay?

647
00:35:31,807 --> 00:35:33,007
You little...

648
00:35:33,007 --> 00:35:34,174
Stop it! No!

649
00:35:34,174 --> 00:35:35,974
You little punk!

650
00:35:37,946 --> 00:35:39,410
You little punk!

651
00:35:39,410 --> 00:35:40,630
Seriously, you...

652
00:35:40,630 --> 00:35:41,707
Hey, come here!

653
00:35:41,707 --> 00:35:42,741
[Pancake Mix]
Come here.

654
00:35:42,741 --> 00:35:44,346
You little punk!

655
00:35:44,346 --> 00:35:47,141
How dare you do this here?

656
00:36:06,474 --> 00:36:10,374
Well, I guess she's
the only person in the world

657
00:36:10,374 --> 00:36:11,694
who can actually chew Yoo Bo Na out.

658
00:36:11,694 --> 00:36:15,074
There's always something new
to learn and master.

659
00:36:15,074 --> 00:36:16,910
That's what running a household is like.

660
00:36:16,910 --> 00:36:19,507
You just have to break through
them again. What can you do?

661
00:36:19,507 --> 00:36:21,622
Just grind it out with sheer effort.

662
00:36:21,622 --> 00:36:25,341
Well, sometimes no amount of effort
can get you through something.

663
00:36:25,341 --> 00:36:29,307
Jeez, that old lady really never changes.

664
00:36:29,307 --> 00:36:32,414
It's about time she showed a bit of mercy.

665
00:36:32,414 --> 00:36:34,746
Will it get better as more time passes?

666
00:36:34,746 --> 00:36:38,974
Yeah, after all that rubbing
each other the wrong way,

667
00:36:39,603 --> 00:36:44,830
laughing and crying together,
physically clashing and hurting each other,

668
00:36:44,830 --> 00:36:47,786
time piles up until it becomes
that thick, sticky bond

669
00:36:47,786 --> 00:36:50,441
we call family.

670
00:36:53,106 --> 00:36:55,141
I guess that's why it's so hard.

671
00:36:57,623 --> 00:37:01,294
<i>Sometimes I find it fascinating,
and sometimes I'm jealous.</i>

672
00:37:01,294 --> 00:37:04,974
<i>Because I've never had anything like that.</i>

673
00:37:06,896 --> 00:37:09,834
Mom! Tae Seong!

674
00:37:09,834 --> 00:37:10,834
Tae Seong!

675
00:37:10,834 --> 00:37:14,307
Yul! Yul is missing!

676
00:37:16,014 --> 00:37:17,714
Bo Na...

677
00:37:18,822 --> 00:37:20,122
Yul!

678
00:37:20,122 --> 00:37:21,686
- Yul!
- Yul...

679
00:37:21,686 --> 00:37:23,638
- You look for her too! Hurry!
- Mom.

680
00:37:23,638 --> 00:37:24,638
Oh, she's not here.

681
00:37:24,638 --> 00:37:26,762
- Yul!
- Is she not there?

682
00:37:26,762 --> 00:37:27,990
- She's not there?
- No.

683
00:37:27,990 --> 00:37:30,262
- What do I do?
- Go check over there.

684
00:37:30,262 --> 00:37:32,074
Yul!

685
00:37:32,074 --> 00:37:33,906
Here? Was she here?

686
00:37:33,906 --> 00:37:35,574
Kwon Se Ah, are you sure you lost her here?

687
00:37:35,574 --> 00:37:41,357
Yeah! I was... I was sitting right here,
and Yul was playing over there.

688
00:37:41,357 --> 00:37:44,574
Chiba! Chiba's leash
came loose, and it ran off,

689
00:37:44,574 --> 00:37:49,141
so I went after it and came back,
but Yul was gone.

690
00:37:49,141 --> 00:37:51,341
Oh, seriously, this kid...

691
00:37:51,341 --> 00:37:52,846
- Yul!
- Oh, for goodness' sake.

692
00:37:52,846 --> 00:37:55,626
Come on, stop crying, you girl.
It's driving me crazy, seriously.

693
00:37:55,626 --> 00:37:58,078
Hey, you take her
and go back inside the house.

694
00:37:58,078 --> 00:38:01,258
Clean up the mess in there.

695
00:38:01,258 --> 00:38:04,241
Mom, is that really what you say
to a mom who's just lost her child?

696
00:38:05,266 --> 00:38:07,730
Yeah, okay. Got it, Tae Seong.

697
00:38:07,730 --> 00:38:11,890
Yeah, when he gets there,
check the CCTV and call me.

698
00:38:11,890 --> 00:38:14,130
It's Tae Seong. He couldn't reach
the security guard earlier,

699
00:38:14,130 --> 00:38:16,010
but he just got through,
and the guard is on his way.

700
00:38:16,010 --> 00:38:19,454
Let's split up and search
the area for now, okay?

701
00:38:19,454 --> 00:38:20,654
Split up. Go.

702
00:38:20,654 --> 00:38:22,330
You go that way. I'll check over there.

703
00:38:22,330 --> 00:38:24,174
That way...

704
00:38:31,234 --> 00:38:32,370
Ms. Yoo!

705
00:38:32,370 --> 00:38:33,626
Oh, Assistant Manager Ki!

706
00:38:33,626 --> 00:38:35,382
You got here sooner than I expected.

707
00:38:35,382 --> 00:38:36,710
Thank you so much for coming.

708
00:38:36,710 --> 00:38:38,294
You said you lost a child, so...

709
00:38:38,294 --> 00:38:40,441
What do I do?

710
00:38:40,441 --> 00:38:42,006
- This...
- That one?

711
00:38:42,006 --> 00:38:45,210
Yeah, can you do it? Is it possible?

712
00:38:45,210 --> 00:38:48,830
So this is what it means
to feel chills and get goosebumps.

713
00:38:48,830 --> 00:38:50,674
I'm counting on you.

714
00:38:51,502 --> 00:38:53,409
Where on earth is she?

715
00:38:53,409 --> 00:38:55,541
Jeez, I'm going crazy.

716
00:38:57,318 --> 00:38:59,407
Oh, Bo Na...

717
00:39:04,330 --> 00:39:05,430
- Se Ah.
- Bo Na.

718
00:39:05,430 --> 00:39:06,902
Se Ah, what's the situation?

719
00:39:06,902 --> 00:39:08,278
Did you check Seo Yeon's place?

720
00:39:08,278 --> 00:39:10,074
Well, they said she never came there either.

721
00:39:10,074 --> 00:39:13,964
And... I didn't see her on the way here.

722
00:39:13,964 --> 00:39:18,607
I'm so sorry, Bo Na.
I should've been watching her better.

723
00:39:20,306 --> 00:39:21,507
We'll find her.

724
00:39:21,507 --> 00:39:24,166
Yul is a smart girl. She'll be okay.

725
00:39:24,166 --> 00:39:25,866
It's okay.

726
00:39:31,170 --> 00:39:34,414
But who is that?

727
00:39:34,414 --> 00:39:38,074
Oh, he's a coworker of mine.

728
00:39:38,074 --> 00:39:39,274
Hacking is his hobby,

729
00:39:39,274 --> 00:39:42,907
so I asked him to see if he could
access those CCTV cameras.

730
00:39:42,907 --> 00:39:46,175
And you know this
has to stay a secret, right?

731
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:50,450
Yes, I've never met a hacker
in real life before.

732
00:39:50,450 --> 00:39:51,618
It's done.

733
00:39:51,618 --> 00:39:53,807
Huh?

734
00:39:56,270 --> 00:39:58,410
What's the exact time the child went missing?

735
00:39:58,410 --> 00:40:02,141
Sometime between 6:30 p.m. and 7 p.m.

736
00:40:04,398 --> 00:40:06,098
I found her.

737
00:40:16,562 --> 00:40:20,807
Luckily, no one took her.
She left on her own.

738
00:40:21,698 --> 00:40:23,398
Thank goodness.

739
00:40:24,446 --> 00:40:26,986
She seems to have wandered
around the apartment complex,

740
00:40:26,986 --> 00:40:32,106
then left the complex
and headed toward the main road.

741
00:40:32,106 --> 00:40:33,426
The main road?

742
00:40:33,426 --> 00:40:36,554
Then I'll check that way.
Let me know if you find anything.

743
00:40:36,554 --> 00:40:38,254
Oh...

744
00:40:43,362 --> 00:40:47,274
Were you the one
who was with her until the end?

745
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:50,158
Yes.

746
00:40:50,158 --> 00:40:52,302
Do you remember anything?

747
00:40:52,302 --> 00:40:55,719
Anything strange about what she said or did?

748
00:40:55,719 --> 00:40:59,755
Oh, well...

749
00:40:59,755 --> 00:41:01,684
Take your time and think.

750
00:41:01,684 --> 00:41:05,407
Even the smallest thing could be a clue.

751
00:41:07,246 --> 00:41:12,186
Yul was asking me a lot of questions.

752
00:41:12,186 --> 00:41:14,726
Auntie, how do you get to heaven?

753
00:41:14,726 --> 00:41:16,594
Heaven? You have to die to go there.

754
00:41:16,594 --> 00:41:19,706
Die, die!

755
00:41:19,706 --> 00:41:24,215
Oh, no! I must've been crazy!

756
00:41:24,215 --> 00:41:28,307
She asked how to get to heaven.

757
00:41:28,307 --> 00:41:31,762
I told her you have to die.

758
00:41:31,762 --> 00:41:33,906
Oh, what do I do?

759
00:41:33,906 --> 00:41:35,407
Why would you say something like that?

760
00:41:35,407 --> 00:41:37,462
Well...

761
00:41:37,462 --> 00:41:41,964
Yul asked me what the ancestral rite is,

762
00:41:41,964 --> 00:41:47,374
and I told her people come down
from heaven to have a meal...

763
00:41:48,882 --> 00:41:50,807
Oh, my...

764
00:41:50,807 --> 00:41:53,990
This is all my fault.

765
00:41:53,990 --> 00:41:57,641
I was stupid enough
to take my eyes off my niece.

766
00:41:58,282 --> 00:42:02,150
Yul, I'm so sorry.

767
00:42:02,150 --> 00:42:05,146
Stop crying. I think I've found a clue.

768
00:42:05,146 --> 00:42:06,307
What?

769
00:42:06,307 --> 00:42:08,323
Yul going missing isn't your fault.

770
00:42:08,323 --> 00:42:11,741
So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.

771
00:42:22,418 --> 00:42:23,494
Tae Seong!

772
00:42:23,494 --> 00:42:25,862
- Honey!
- Where's Yul?

773
00:42:25,862 --> 00:42:29,698
Well... We'll find Yul soon,
so I don't think you need to worry too much.

774
00:42:29,698 --> 00:42:32,474
Yul went toward the main road, right?

775
00:42:33,282 --> 00:42:35,774
How did you know...

776
00:42:35,864 --> 00:42:37,119
[Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do]

777
00:42:37,582 --> 00:42:39,774
Yeah, Assistant Manager Ki,
what did you find?

778
00:42:41,170 --> 00:42:42,870
What?

779
00:42:46,650 --> 00:42:48,458
She was looking up at the sky.

780
00:42:48,458 --> 00:42:50,946
So there must've been something
in the sky, right?

781
00:42:50,946 --> 00:42:53,694
<i>Judging by the slight movement of her head,</i>

782
00:42:53,694 --> 00:42:55,362
<i>I think it might have been an airplane.</i>

783
00:42:55,362 --> 00:42:56,705
<i>Oh? That's right!</i>

784
00:42:56,705 --> 00:42:59,141
<i>Flights to Gimpo fly over our neighborhood.</i>

785
00:42:59,141 --> 00:43:00,958
Yul loves watching planes,

786
00:43:00,958 --> 00:43:04,218
so sometimes I take her up
to Tae Seong's rooftop...

787
00:43:04,218 --> 00:43:05,941
Oh, my!

788
00:43:11,478 --> 00:43:17,374
From what you said, it seems Yul
wanted to go to heaven for some reason.

789
00:43:44,242 --> 00:43:46,474
I'll get the key.

790
00:43:48,086 --> 00:43:49,786
Yeah.

791
00:43:52,641 --> 00:43:56,010
Take me with you!

792
00:43:56,010 --> 00:43:58,450
Take me with you!

793
00:43:58,450 --> 00:44:00,962
Take me with you too.

794
00:44:00,962 --> 00:44:04,286
Take me with you!

795
00:44:04,286 --> 00:44:07,173
Take me with you.

796
00:44:07,173 --> 00:44:12,127
Come here, and take me with you.

797
00:44:12,127 --> 00:44:15,841
<i>I think she thought the airplane
would take her there.</i>

798
00:44:17,714 --> 00:44:21,335
It was left open for waterproofing work
earlier today, but I locked it just now.

799
00:44:21,335 --> 00:44:25,207
Oh, my God. What on earth happened?

800
00:44:33,582 --> 00:44:35,322
Huh?

801
00:44:35,322 --> 00:44:38,774
Who told you to come up here alone? Huh?
Is that what I taught you?

802
00:44:38,774 --> 00:44:40,506
Are you going to wander around
by yourself at night like this?

803
00:44:40,506 --> 00:44:42,398
Why did you come up here
in the middle of the night?

804
00:44:42,398 --> 00:44:45,941
Are you hurt anywhere?
Are you going to do that again?

805
00:44:47,026 --> 00:44:49,666
I was going to bring them back.

806
00:44:49,666 --> 00:44:51,906
Who? Bring who back?

807
00:44:51,906 --> 00:44:54,574
Mommy's mom and dad.

808
00:44:55,438 --> 00:44:59,341
I heard they went to heaven.

809
00:45:01,266 --> 00:45:05,407
I was going to bring them back on a plane.

810
00:45:06,415 --> 00:45:09,634
Because Mommy is an orphan.

811
00:45:09,634 --> 00:45:13,574
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

812
00:45:25,610 --> 00:45:28,918
I see. I'm sorry. I...

813
00:45:28,918 --> 00:45:31,726
I didn't know how you felt
and scolded you first. I'm sorry.

814
00:45:31,726 --> 00:45:33,043
Don't cry, Yul. Come here.

815
00:45:33,043 --> 00:45:35,341
I'm sorry. Mommy's sorry.

816
00:45:36,850 --> 00:45:39,241
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have done that.

817
00:46:09,802 --> 00:46:10,994
Are you okay?

818
00:46:10,994 --> 00:46:12,694
Huh?

819
00:46:14,182 --> 00:46:16,270
I'm okay.

820
00:46:16,270 --> 00:46:19,032
Anyway, we found Yul safely.

821
00:46:19,032 --> 00:46:20,778
I'm sorry.

822
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:24,222
But how could you do that to me?

823
00:46:24,222 --> 00:46:28,498
How could you imagine me
suddenly disappearing one day?

824
00:46:28,498 --> 00:46:30,474
How could you imagine such a thing?

825
00:46:31,298 --> 00:46:32,998
Huh?

826
00:46:34,750 --> 00:46:38,058
When you have something precious,
like an expensive jewel,

827
00:46:38,058 --> 00:46:40,170
you're always afraid of losing it.

828
00:46:40,170 --> 00:46:42,469
That's what you are to me.

829
00:46:42,469 --> 00:46:45,241
You're so precious to me...

830
00:46:46,446 --> 00:46:48,807
that I'm afraid I'll lose you.

831
00:47:00,141 --> 00:47:04,526
I mean, you're not usually like this,
so why today...

832
00:47:04,526 --> 00:47:06,398
I don't know. You're in big trouble now.

833
00:47:06,398 --> 00:47:08,974
You totally lost points with Mother.

834
00:47:10,174 --> 00:47:14,007
Well, I can just earn double the points
I lost with Mom from you.

835
00:47:16,682 --> 00:47:20,042
No, I definitely lost a lot of points today.

836
00:47:20,042 --> 00:47:23,226
Because of me,
the ancestral rites were canceled.

837
00:47:23,226 --> 00:47:26,441
But we all decided that by vote, so whatever.

838
00:47:29,770 --> 00:47:32,714
Our Yul really did something big today.

839
00:47:32,714 --> 00:47:36,974
She even softened Grandma's stubborn heart.

840
00:47:36,974 --> 00:47:39,654
My daughter is better than I.

841
00:47:39,654 --> 00:47:42,407
She even comforted her mommy's heart.

842
00:47:46,362 --> 00:47:49,974
I'm supposed to be the one
comforting my daughter.

843
00:47:50,750 --> 00:47:53,952
She's still so young.

844
00:47:53,952 --> 00:47:57,607
I wish she didn't have to
understand things like that yet.

845
00:48:21,390 --> 00:48:23,090
Oh, dear.

846
00:48:24,118 --> 00:48:27,966
She's a mom too, so she went
completely crazy over her own kid.

847
00:48:27,966 --> 00:48:29,742
But still, that's too much.

848
00:48:29,742 --> 00:48:32,574
Still, how can she glare
at her mother-in-law like that?

849
00:48:34,302 --> 00:48:37,307
Because Mommy is an orphan.

850
00:48:38,315 --> 00:48:41,964
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

851
00:48:41,964 --> 00:48:43,978
Is it because she's an orphan?

852
00:48:43,978 --> 00:48:48,241
She does seem especially attached
when it comes to her family.

853
00:48:51,514 --> 00:48:53,307
Looks like...

854
00:48:55,239 --> 00:48:58,066
Bo Na is pretty athletic, huh?

855
00:48:58,066 --> 00:49:00,322
You little punk!

856
00:49:00,322 --> 00:49:02,038
No wonder.

857
00:49:02,038 --> 00:49:04,807
Did she do sports
or something back in school?

858
00:49:07,950 --> 00:49:10,758
But why has she been
spacing out since earlier?

859
00:49:10,758 --> 00:49:13,941
<i>So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.</i>

860
00:49:28,397 --> 00:49:29,578
What?

861
00:49:29,578 --> 00:49:31,278
What's wrong with her?

862
00:49:32,662 --> 00:49:35,474
She must still be shaken up from losing Yul.

863
00:49:37,952 --> 00:49:42,674
Anyway, I'm so relieved the ancestral rites
are over as of today!

864
00:49:43,315 --> 00:49:45,264
What an ungrateful bunch!

865
00:49:45,264 --> 00:49:47,702
You don't care about your mom one bit.

866
00:49:47,702 --> 00:49:50,686
Oh, our dear Ok Seon Ja, what's wrong now?

867
00:49:50,686 --> 00:49:53,207
If there's no ancestral rite,
you're the one who'll have it easiest.

868
00:49:53,207 --> 00:49:55,644
Easy for you to say.

869
00:49:55,644 --> 00:49:57,654
I've done this my whole life.

870
00:49:57,654 --> 00:50:01,731
If we abolish it now,
how am I supposed to face our ancestors?

871
00:50:01,731 --> 00:50:03,926
Oh, Mom!

872
00:50:03,926 --> 00:50:05,562
It's settled.
Why are you bringing it up again?

873
00:50:05,562 --> 00:50:10,278
We voted on whether to abolish it,
and the majority voted yes.

874
00:50:10,278 --> 00:50:12,374
That's it! Done! Over!

875
00:50:13,301 --> 00:50:17,214
Let's go clean up that mess over there.

876
00:50:17,214 --> 00:50:20,407
Oh, my, when are we ever
going to clean all that up?

877
00:50:21,182 --> 00:50:22,556
You godless bunch!

878
00:50:22,556 --> 00:50:26,774
Just you wait!
I'll do it all by myself next year.

879
00:50:37,954 --> 00:50:40,730
By the way, what was the vote count?

880
00:50:40,730 --> 00:50:42,206
- Huh?
- You counted the votes.

881
00:50:42,206 --> 00:50:44,450
You're the only one who saw the results.

882
00:50:44,450 --> 00:50:47,674
Well, obviously,
Mom was the one vote against it.

883
00:50:49,686 --> 00:50:51,641
That's...

884
00:51:01,742 --> 00:51:03,726
a secret.

885
00:51:03,726 --> 00:51:05,202
Why?

886
00:51:05,202 --> 00:51:06,974
Tell me, please.

887
00:51:06,974 --> 00:51:10,577
We agreed to keep the vote count secret.

888
00:51:10,577 --> 00:51:12,574
But tell me.

889
00:51:12,574 --> 00:51:15,024
Fine, I'm going to sulk.

890
00:51:15,024 --> 00:51:16,466
What's wrong?

891
00:51:16,466 --> 00:51:18,682
Please don't talk to me.

892
00:51:18,682 --> 00:51:22,274
And I don't think I'll get over this easily.

893
00:51:24,362 --> 00:51:27,586
Please tell me! Please!

894
00:51:27,586 --> 00:51:29,241
- Are you really that curious?
- Yeah.

895
00:51:29,241 --> 00:51:31,041
I guess you would be.

896
00:51:31,041 --> 00:51:33,341
Come on, really?

897
00:51:39,908 --> 00:51:42,017
Help me!

898
00:51:42,017 --> 00:51:44,317
Help me! Please, over here!

899
00:51:44,317 --> 00:51:46,051
I'm falling! Help me!

900
00:51:46,051 --> 00:51:47,751
Help me!

901
00:51:47,751 --> 00:51:50,251
Help me! Please!

902
00:52:01,737 --> 00:52:04,768
We've determined that Tak Jong Gu
spends his time going back and forth

903
00:52:04,768 --> 00:52:09,608
between the 22nd-floor VIP gaming room
and the 23rd-floor VIP suite.

904
00:52:09,608 --> 00:52:14,072
His dad has forbidden him from leaving,
so he can't go outside

905
00:52:14,072 --> 00:52:16,620
and takes care of everything
inside this building.

906
00:52:16,620 --> 00:52:19,799
And since the gaming room is a sealed,
windowless space,

907
00:52:19,799 --> 00:52:22,404
he can't be sniped from outside.

908
00:52:22,404 --> 00:52:26,164
So that means we'd have to target him
while he's inside his suite.

909
00:52:26,164 --> 00:52:27,864
The problem is that...

910
00:52:29,056 --> 00:52:33,496
Tak Jong Gu's room, 2305,
is on this side of the building.

911
00:52:33,496 --> 00:52:36,552
As you can see, the front window
has a completely open view.

912
00:52:36,552 --> 00:52:40,651
And the convention center next door
is almost directly opposite it.

913
00:52:41,300 --> 00:52:44,425
So there's no angle for a sniper shot.

914
00:52:44,425 --> 00:52:48,817
Then we'd have to lure him outside first.

915
00:52:48,817 --> 00:52:52,986
So the only way for us to get close is
through the 22nd-floor gaming room?

916
00:52:52,986 --> 00:52:55,112
<i>The 22nd-floor gaming room is for VIPs only,</i>

917
00:52:55,112 --> 00:52:57,708
<i>so ordinary guests can't access it.</i>

918
00:52:57,708 --> 00:53:02,417
<i>There is, however, one way
for ordinary guests to get in.</i>

919
00:53:03,284 --> 00:53:04,980
<i>Every day, the person</i>

920
00:53:04,980 --> 00:53:08,552
<i>who wins the most chips
in the first-floor public gaming room</i>

921
00:53:08,552 --> 00:53:10,573
<i>gets a pass to the VIP gaming room.</i>

922
00:53:10,573 --> 00:53:13,451
<i>It's basically a one-day pass.</i>

923
00:53:15,599 --> 00:53:18,776
So they expect you to win downstairs
and lose it all upstairs.

924
00:53:18,776 --> 00:53:21,712
We're barely covering
operating expenses this month.

925
00:53:21,712 --> 00:53:24,674
So, one of us just needs to
pose as a customer

926
00:53:24,674 --> 00:53:29,199
and to win that VIP pass.

927
00:53:29,199 --> 00:53:32,832
Tak Jong Gu mainly plays blackjack.

928
00:53:32,832 --> 00:53:35,117
Anyone here know how to play blackjack?

929
00:53:36,203 --> 00:53:37,652
I've never played blackjack before.

930
00:53:37,652 --> 00:53:38,780
Then what games have you played?

931
00:53:38,780 --> 00:53:39,953
One Card.

932
00:53:39,953 --> 00:53:41,092
One Card?

933
00:53:41,092 --> 00:53:42,360
Is that any fun?

934
00:53:42,360 --> 00:53:44,060
No one?

935
00:53:47,628 --> 00:53:51,351
Has anyone ever won money playing blackjack?

936
00:54:13,006 --> 00:54:17,748
In blackjack, the player whose cards
total 21 or come closest to 21 wins,

937
00:54:17,748 --> 00:54:19,940
giving the dealer and player
roughly equal odds.

938
00:54:19,940 --> 00:54:23,617
So I created a program
that maximizes those odds.

939
00:54:24,761 --> 00:54:27,296
These glasses have the program
built into them.

940
00:54:27,296 --> 00:54:29,420
They recognize the cards that
have been played and those remaining,

941
00:54:29,420 --> 00:54:33,584
<i>and then signal whether I should
hit or stay with lights only I can see.</i>

942
00:54:42,858 --> 00:54:46,164
Congratulations.
This is your pass to the VIP gaming room.

943
00:54:46,164 --> 00:54:47,864
Thank you.

944
00:54:57,924 --> 00:55:01,584
<i>So we'll get the VIP pass
this way, go upstairs,</i>

945
00:55:02,591 --> 00:55:04,298
<i>and approach Tak Jong Gu.</i>

946
00:55:04,298 --> 00:55:07,884
<i>We'll drop a pill into his drink.</i>

947
00:55:08,556 --> 00:55:10,380
It's a drug that causes vasculitis.

948
00:55:10,380 --> 00:55:14,988
<i>A few minutes after he takes it,
red spots will break out all over his body.</i>

949
00:55:14,988 --> 00:55:16,672
Get a doctor now!

950
00:55:16,672 --> 00:55:19,064
Get the doctor!

951
00:55:19,064 --> 00:55:22,528
<i>That's when Manager Go will appear
disguised as the on-site doctor.</i>

952
00:55:22,528 --> 00:55:24,640
Hey! What's this?

953
00:55:24,640 --> 00:55:26,028
It's an acute allergic reaction.

954
00:55:26,028 --> 00:55:27,896
You could go into shock
if we leave you like this.

955
00:55:27,896 --> 00:55:29,984
We need to get you to a hospital right away.

956
00:55:33,992 --> 00:55:36,451
<i>Once we get Tak Jong Gu outside, we're done.</i>

957
00:55:58,351 --> 00:56:01,616
[Hongseon Rest Area]

958
00:56:01,616 --> 00:56:03,744
He didn't fall while working,

959
00:56:03,744 --> 00:56:07,024
so why was he there in the middle
of the night, and how did he fall?

960
00:56:07,024 --> 00:56:10,324
And from the exact same spot
where Kang Yeong Ho fell to his death.

961
00:56:10,324 --> 00:56:12,520
What does the police say?

962
00:56:12,520 --> 00:56:14,328
Looks like they don't have
any answers either.

963
00:56:14,328 --> 00:56:17,156
It was late at night in a remote area,
so there were no witnesses.

964
00:56:17,156 --> 00:56:19,460
Wow, but that Park Chun Bok guy,

965
00:56:19,460 --> 00:56:22,088
he acted like such a saint
during the interview.

966
00:56:22,088 --> 00:56:23,966
But he had assault, theft,
and even attempted murder on his record.

967
00:56:23,966 --> 00:56:26,964
A whopping five-time ex-con!

968
00:56:26,964 --> 00:56:29,956
You really can't judge a person
by appearances.

969
00:56:29,956 --> 00:56:34,724
And before he died, he was handing out money
from some unknown source?

970
00:56:34,724 --> 00:56:38,353
This feels like a terrifying case
involving Chairman Cheon Seong Gil,

971
00:56:38,353 --> 00:56:39,676
the field workers, and everyone in between.

972
00:56:39,676 --> 00:56:43,072
It seems like a complex and terrifying case.

973
00:56:43,072 --> 00:56:45,333
Anyway, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
is at the center of it.

974
00:56:45,333 --> 00:56:47,451
Let's go meet him first.

975
00:56:48,704 --> 00:56:51,548
Do you think he'll see us?
He already refused our interview.

976
00:56:51,548 --> 00:56:53,804
Who says we have to do a formal interview?

977
00:56:53,804 --> 00:56:55,504
Oh!

978
00:57:02,764 --> 00:57:04,508
Seven.

979
00:57:04,508 --> 00:57:06,703
Hit.

980
00:57:06,703 --> 00:57:08,417
Thirteen.

981
00:57:12,518 --> 00:57:14,251
Stay.

982
00:57:15,264 --> 00:57:16,336
Fourteen.

983
00:57:16,336 --> 00:57:18,384
Twenty-four, bust.

984
00:57:24,464 --> 00:57:26,164
Eighteen.

985
00:57:27,284 --> 00:57:28,984
Stay.

986
00:57:42,928 --> 00:57:44,651
Eleven.

987
00:57:46,596 --> 00:57:48,616
- Down.
- Double down.

988
00:57:48,616 --> 00:57:49,686
[Double Down: Double your bet
and get one more card]

989
00:57:52,090 --> 00:57:53,684
Twenty-three. Dealer bust.

990
00:57:53,684 --> 00:57:55,352
[Bust: The total exceeds 21]

991
00:57:55,596 --> 00:57:57,533
Twenty-one.

992
00:57:57,533 --> 00:58:00,884
Congratulations. Your double down paid off.

993
00:58:03,274 --> 00:58:04,748
- Nice, blackjack!
- Blackjack!

994
00:58:04,748 --> 00:58:06,136
Congratulations!

995
00:58:06,136 --> 00:58:07,817
Would you like to take even money?

996
00:58:07,817 --> 00:58:09,052
[Even Money: If the dealer
might also have blackjack,]

997
00:58:09,052 --> 00:58:09,641
[you give up the 1.5:1 payout
and take 1:1 instead. A kind of insurance]

998
00:58:10,292 --> 00:58:12,048
Sure.

999
00:58:12,048 --> 00:58:14,476
Oh, come on.

1000
00:58:14,476 --> 00:58:16,751
Don't do that.

1001
00:58:18,068 --> 00:58:20,796
You've got to go for it here,
even if you might lose.

1002
00:58:20,796 --> 00:58:23,584
Are you new to gambling?

1003
00:58:28,960 --> 00:58:30,620
Eighteen.

1004
00:58:30,620 --> 00:58:33,117
See? You barely won anything.

1005
00:58:33,117 --> 00:58:36,384
Making pennies like that,
when are you ever going to get rich?

1006
00:58:39,084 --> 00:58:42,603
Still, that's a decent win
for someone so chicken-hearted, huh?

1007
00:58:42,603 --> 00:58:45,384
Would you like to join the game, ma'am?

1008
00:58:46,308 --> 00:58:48,391
Me?

1009
00:58:48,391 --> 00:58:50,754
Oh, jeez.

1010
00:58:50,754 --> 00:58:53,784
I really shouldn't do this.

1011
00:58:55,036 --> 00:58:58,617
I really quit gambling.

1012
00:59:06,684 --> 00:59:07,841
[Gaecheon Construction]

1013
00:59:12,080 --> 00:59:16,484
Huh? Isn't that Chairman Cheon's car?

1014
00:59:28,748 --> 00:59:31,484
Looks like he's going somewhere.
What do we do?

1015
00:59:32,696 --> 00:59:35,908
What do you mean? We have to follow him.

1016
00:59:35,908 --> 00:59:37,617
Again?

1017
00:59:42,528 --> 00:59:43,584
Seventeen.

1018
00:59:43,584 --> 00:59:45,133
- Yes!
- Wow!

1019
00:59:45,133 --> 00:59:47,251
How many wins is that?

1020
00:59:55,364 --> 00:59:58,223
It's been so long
since I've felt this thrill.

1021
00:59:58,223 --> 01:00:01,784
Okay, from now on,

1022
01:00:01,784 --> 01:00:04,024
[Three Hands: One person plays three hands]
should I go three hands?

1023
01:00:04,024 --> 01:00:06,874
- Join?
- I'm good.

1024
01:00:06,874 --> 01:00:08,372
Chicken.

1025
01:00:08,372 --> 01:00:10,651
[Pair: First two cards have the same value]
I'm betting on a pair too.

1026
01:00:11,864 --> 01:00:13,651
No more bets?

1027
01:00:22,184 --> 01:00:24,208
Nice pair.

1028
01:00:24,208 --> 01:00:25,908
Yes!

1029
01:00:28,032 --> 01:00:30,274
Yeah.

1030
01:00:30,274 --> 01:00:31,344
Congratulations!

1031
01:00:31,344 --> 01:00:34,056
This is a pass granting
you access to the VIP gaming room.

1032
01:00:34,056 --> 01:00:37,016
Wow, thank you!

1033
01:00:37,016 --> 01:00:39,637
Thank you! Thank you!

1034
01:00:39,637 --> 01:00:41,384
Thank you!

1035
01:00:48,694 --> 01:00:50,632
Good job, chicken.

1036
01:00:50,632 --> 01:00:52,672
You should quit while you're ahead.

1037
01:00:52,672 --> 01:00:55,517
You'll lose everything otherwise.

1038
01:00:59,220 --> 01:01:00,312
See you around!

1039
01:01:06,416 --> 01:01:08,711
Oh, I lost!

1040
01:01:08,711 --> 01:01:11,149
I lost again!

1041
01:01:11,149 --> 01:01:13,788
Mister, I lost again.

1042
01:01:13,788 --> 01:01:16,884
I lost again!

1043
01:01:18,804 --> 01:01:20,504
What are you doing here again?

1044
01:01:23,249 --> 01:01:25,324
Even your plans fail sometimes.

1045
01:01:25,324 --> 01:01:27,384
I'm sorry, Ms. Yoo.

1046
01:01:30,725 --> 01:01:34,512
But there are always
unexpected variables in the field.

1047
01:01:34,512 --> 01:01:38,521
And cleaning up after a junior's mistakes
is part of being a good senior.

1048
01:01:38,521 --> 01:01:40,817
What are you thinking?

1049
01:01:40,817 --> 01:01:42,060
I'm thinking maybe I should go in directly.

1050
01:01:42,060 --> 01:01:44,152
You, personally?

1051
01:01:44,152 --> 01:01:45,324
The gaming room might be difficult,

1052
01:01:45,324 --> 01:01:47,860
but wouldn't it be easier
to sneak into his suite?

1053
01:01:47,860 --> 01:01:50,048
I'll just drug his water and get out.

1054
01:01:50,048 --> 01:01:52,288
That's our best option right now.

1055
01:01:52,288 --> 01:01:53,712
I can't agree to that.

1056
01:01:53,712 --> 01:01:55,717
It's too dangerous for you
to expose yourself on-site.

1057
01:01:55,717 --> 01:01:58,580
You will back me up, won't you?

1058
01:01:58,580 --> 01:01:59,796
- Well, that's...
- Tell Manager Go

1059
01:01:59,796 --> 01:02:02,651
about the revised plan beforehand.

1060
01:02:04,392 --> 01:02:06,772
Okay, shall we go?

1061
01:02:06,772 --> 01:02:08,472
Ms. Yoo.

1062
01:02:09,456 --> 01:02:12,451
You know your safety comes first, right?

1063
01:02:19,844 --> 01:02:21,351
No, wait a moment.

1064
01:02:21,351 --> 01:02:22,699
Chairman!

1065
01:02:22,699 --> 01:02:27,051
Please, just let me in for a moment!

1066
01:02:27,051 --> 01:02:28,312
Oh, please!

1067
01:02:28,312 --> 01:02:30,284
Just a moment.

1068
01:03:13,726 --> 01:03:17,762
[A Bona Fide Killer]

1069
01:03:17,908 --> 01:03:19,092
How bad is this guy?

1070
01:03:19,092 --> 01:03:21,484
On the surface,
it looks like an accidental mishap,

1071
01:03:21,484 --> 01:03:23,212
but a premeditated murder underneath?

1072
01:03:23,212 --> 01:03:25,510
- Done.
- Someone's coming down the hall.

1073
01:03:25,510 --> 01:03:26,520
A reporter?

1074
01:03:26,520 --> 01:03:28,940
Well, this just got interesting.

1075
01:03:28,940 --> 01:03:31,332
No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.

1076
01:03:31,332 --> 01:03:33,062
That woman could become a witness...

1077
01:03:33,062 --> 01:03:34,591
What's the variable this time?

1078
01:03:34,591 --> 01:03:35,941
Someone else is coming down the hall.

1079
01:03:35,941 --> 01:03:37,984
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

1080
01:03:37,984 --> 01:03:40,956
In the end, the day will come
when that secret is revealed.

1081
01:03:40,956 --> 01:03:43,149
It's all my fault.

1082
01:03:43,149 --> 01:03:46,651
Calm down. Director Yoo will be fine.

1083
01:03:47,268 --> 01:03:48,404
What's wrong?

1084
01:03:48,404 --> 01:03:50,384
It's someone I know.
